==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang}} {{term|ficol|lang=ang}}. From {{proto|Germanic}} (compare Old Norse {{term|feikn||portent}}), from {{proto|Indo-European}} (Latin {{term|piget||it irks, displeases}})

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɪk.əl/}}, {{SAMPA|/fIk.@l/}}
*: {{audio|en-us-fickle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪkəl}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Quick to change one’s [[opinion]] or [[allegiance]]; [[insincere]]; not [[loyal]] or [[reliable]].

Also known as Call of Duty PC Players who moan and moan that they want Custom Maps and choice of Server hosts.
Then go straight out and buy COD Black Ops, So that the COD don't give a flying F, As they now have your money = Fickle

